[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Rousseau Gambit"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit: 4.exf5 e4"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "hanging-piece,trap"]
[Themes "tempo-gain,piece-activity"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5 4. exf5 4... e4 { Hits the knight and opens the diagonal for the queen. White's knight must move, and Black gains time. [%cal Ge4f3] }
5. Nd4 (5. Ng5? 5... Qxg5 { The knight has no defender, and the queen takes it for nothing. } 6. O-O 6... Qxf5) (5. Ne5? 5... Nxe5 6. Bb5 6... c6) 5... Nf6 { Develops with a threat of a quick ...d5 to hit the bishop. The knight on d4 is also attacked by the c6 knight. } 6. Nxc6 6... dxc6 { Opens the d-file and the bishop on c8. } 7. d3 7... Bxf5 { Takes the pawn back and develops with a good position. } 8. dxe4 8... Qxd1+ { Trades queens and forces White's king to recapture, so White can no longer castle. } 9. Kxd1 9... O-O-O+ { Check on the open d-file, and it brings the rook into play with the pawn on e4 still to be won back. [%cal Gd8d1] } 10. Ke1 10... Nxe4 *
